# crew#88 documentation standard: every document has an owner, and GitHub enforces review on the
# same rows. One GitHub user exists in this estate today, so every row names the founder; the rows
# are split by area so a second owner is one line, not a rewrite. The last matching row wins.
# science/docsmap.py (crew) reads this file when a document carries no Owner: line.
*                       @chidionyema
/platform/              @chidionyema
/clusters/              @chidionyema
/backstage/             @chidionyema
/catalog/               @chidionyema
/docs/                  @chidionyema
/bin/                   @chidionyema
/tests/                 @chidionyema
/.github/               @chidionyema

# The gateway verifies everyone else; it cannot verify itself. verifier.yml, its engine,
# and the spec that defines it require the founder's review so an agent cannot weaken the
# gate in the same PR that needs weakening. (docs/specs/2026-09-22-cryptographic-ci-gateway.md §3)
/.github/workflows/verifier.yml       @chidionyema
/sovereign/verifier.py                @chidionyema
/bin/idp-ci-verify                    @chidionyema
/docs/specs/2026-09-22-cryptographic-ci-gateway.md  @chidionyema
